1006 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 445 0 R
/E (The scatter shows a wide spread with no strong negative correlation the trendline is nearly flat with a very slight positive slope. This is counterintuitive and analytically interesting. It suggests that in this dataset, higher absences do not reliably predict lower grades. Possible explanations include: students who miss school may do so for legitimate medical reasons while maintaining strong academic standing, or the most academically disengaged students simply have low grades regardless of absence count. This finding challenges the assumption that attendance alone determines performance and is worth highlighting explicitly in your report as it demonstrates genuine analytical insight. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
